<title>USA: Proxim Q4 shr $0.31 including gain.</title>
<headline>Proxim Q4 shr $0.31 including gain.</headline>
<dateline>MOUNTAIN VIEW, Calif. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Proxim, Inc.</p>
<p>				Statement of Operations</p>
<p>		     (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				     Three Months Ended  Year Ended</p>
<p>					    Dec. 31,	  Dec. 31,</p>
<p>					   1996    1995    1996    1995</p>
<p>					 (unaudited)</p>
<p> Revenue			    $11,652  $8,588 $41,220 $22,083</p>
<p> Cost of Revenue		    6,117   4,274  21,383  10,843</p>
<p> Gross profit			 5,535   4,314  19,837  11,240</p>
<p> Research and development	 1,412   1,017   4,949   3,288</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative		    2,593   2,388   9,408   6,694</p>
<p> Income from operations	   1,530     909   5,480   1,258</p>
<p> Interest and other income	2,186     102   2,838     537</p>
<p> Income before income taxes     3,716   1,011   8,318   1,795</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes	423  (1,130)  1,664  (1,051)</p>
<p> Net income			   3,293   2,141   6,654   2,846</p>
<p> Net income per share		0.31    0.26    0.71    0.35</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>					 10,577   8,179   9,386   8,172</p>
<p>NOTES: Net income for the year ended Dec. 31, 1996 was $6,654,000, or $0.71 per share, including a one-time non-operating gain of $1,500,000, or $0.13 per share, related to the November 1996 termination of a proposed merger with DSP Communications Inc.</p>
<p>Net income for the year ended Dec. 31, 1995 was $2,846,000, or $0.35 per share, including a credit of $1,231,000, or $0.15 per share, to recognize the benefit of recording deferred tax assets related to net operating loss carryforwards in accordance with FAS No. 109. The effective annual income tax rate was 20 percent for 1996 and 10 percent for 1995.</p>
<p>Net income for the fourth quarter of 1996 was $3,293,000, or $0.31 per share, including the one-time non-operating gain and an effective tax rate of 11 percent in order to adjust the full year tax rate to 20 percent. Net income for the fourth quarter of 1995 was $2,141,000, or $0.26 per share, including the $0.15 per share tax benefit.</p>
</text>
